es with disordered eating as  always feel free to skip this video if  it's not supportive to your journey and  of course if you are new here do not  forget to subscribe to this channel and  ring that little bell so that you never  miss out on an episode and also follow  me over on tik tok and instagram at  abi's kitchen i also want to say very  clearly that all digestive issues  including bloating are remarkably  complex it was really hard for me to  make this video because the cause of  people's bloating and therefore the  appropriate treatment will be highly  individualized so for example the  recommendations for folks with bloating  from constipation would possibly make  bloating from something like sibo far  worse and vice versa so always speak to  a registered dietitian who specializes  in digestive health about your unique  case in fact i consulted with not one  but four of my gi rd colleagues in this  video to get their clinical insight so a  big thank you to dasha aguilnek amber  gourley caitlyn self and lacy dunn for  all of their help as always i'm going to  be leaving links to their practices  below next i want to quickly flag that  you know diet culture has kind of  co-opted the term bloating to be like a  more pc term for fat it is also  pathologized the very normal experience  of your stomach expanding and  contracting throughout the day this is  wellness culture bs  i'm sorry i'm allergic to bull it is  normal to experience daily gas and it's  normal for your bowel habits to change  in response to certain foods or times of  the month but if you're experiencing  bloating that is very painful linked to  other side effects like nausea where  you're visibly distended to the point  that you maybe look pregnant or it feels  like there's a balloon in there and that  these symptoms seem to be chronic and  persistent every day that's when it's  definitely worth reaching out for help  so in part one we're going to be  discussing the top reasons why you may  be experiencing bloating and then in  part two we're going to be getting into  what to do about it reason number one  food intolerances undiagnosed food  intolerances to things like dairy gluten  or literally any other food that's being  poorly digested and therefore fermenting  in the gut can of course cause excess  gas production and therefore bloating  allergies can also occasionally cause  bloating because the histamine response  can increase mast cell production which  may elevate estrogen which can cause  constipation and that can ultimately  result in bloating but generally  speaking bloating is more of an  intolerance than an allergy symptom  unfortunately while food allergies can  be reliably diagnosed intolerances are a  little more hit and miss those food  sensitivity tests that you see all over  instagram are not evidenced based so an  elimination diet which should be  supervised by a registered dietitian is  really the gold standard of care here  reason number two sensitivity to high  fodmap foods so fodmaps are short chain  carbohydrates that are poorly absorbed  in the small intestine leaving them to  be fermented by bacteria which then  causes gas some of the more common  offenders include foods like cruciferous  veggies beans and legumes dairy wheat as  well as some non-caloric sweeteners  however it's important to note that  sensitivity to high fodmap foods is  highly individualized meaning that you  could be sensitive to certain high  fodmap foods in specific quantities but  able to tolerate others in higher  quantities again this is why it's so  important to be working with a dietitian  to help you eat the greatest variety of  foods with the fewest amount of symptoms  reason number three you're swallowing  too much air what we consume and how we  consume it can increase the amount of  air that we swallow which can build up  in the digestive tract and lead to  uncomfortable gas so things like  drinking carbonated beverages drinking  through a straw chewing a lot of gum  eating while talking or eating in a  hurry can all contribute to the amount  of air entering our bodies and therefore  bloating now reason number four you are  under eating or suffering from an eating  disorder now this is a big topic but  there is a strong correlation between  disordered eating and bloating for a  variety of reasons in short chronically  under eating can reduce stomach acid  production and serotonin levels which  slows motility and it can cause a  sluggish thyroid and it can also cause  gastroparesis which also slows digestion  this often can perpetuate further  disordered eating because people  wrongfully assume that they have food  intolerances because they have symptoms  when they do eat them so they become  more fearful of eating and then eat even  less and this actually just makes the  digestive symptoms worse now this  deserves a whole video in itself so if  that's something of interest definitely  leave me a comment below reason number  five you're not getting enough fiber and  hydration can i get you anything  water would be nice one of the major  causes of bloating is actually  constipation or poor motility if you're  not consuming enough fiber and water to  help your stool move through the bowels  you're gonna get backed up which means  more fermentation and more gas bloating  and distension so you'll want to aim for  at least 25 to 38 grams of fiber per day  depending on sex size and tolerance and  a mix of soluble and insoluble fiber  from foods like fruit veggies whole  grains and other plants and don't forget  that with any fiber you need enough  water to help propel that bulk through  the bowel so making sure that you're  staying hydrated is really important to  preventing yourself getting more backed  up and speaking of backed up reason  number six is you're eating too much  fiber so fiber is a really delicate  balance when it comes to digestion it's  a real goldilocks in the three bears  situation so like the porridge can  easily be too hot or too cold i hate it  when someone messes with my porridge  it's sometimes hard to get it just right  but consuming excess of fiber is usually  accompanied by a heavy load of fodmaps  which can cause fermentation which leads  to gas this is especially an issue if  you're not used to consuming fiber and  you suddenly consume a huge load of it  and perhaps we're just not consuming  enough water to help support it this is  why it's worth working with a  professional for any constipation  related issues because there really can  be some careful trial and error to  ensure that you're getting enough fiber  but not too much to help move the bowels  without excess bulk and that brings me  to reason number seven inadequate  digestive outputs anytime we see someone  make any drastic quick changes to their  diet whether it's you know a crash  weight loss diet or an unsupervised  elimination diet eating disorder etc  there's a risk of normal digestion going  so  [Music]  major fast changes to diet don't allow  your body the time it needs to really  catch up on digestive outputs  like creating the right enzymes or  stomach acid amounts so for example if  you've been dairy free for years and you  suddenly have a big bowl of ice cream  your body has gotten used to not having  to produce the lactase enzyme to break  that down so  yeah it's probably gonna hurt ditto for  folks who've gone vegan and who suddenly  have a 16 ounce steak their body didn't  get the urgent memo in time to produce  enough of the protease enzymes and  stomach acid needed to break that porta  house down so we need to really go slow  to train the gut to upregulate the  enzyme and stomach acid production to  meet the body's changing demands moving  on to reason number eight hormones now  the rise in progesterone hormone leading  up to that time of the month can not  only contribute to the feeling of  bloating from some water retention but  also typically results in constipation  which can further exacerbate symptoms of  gas bloating and abdominal discomfort i  know i'm simplifying this because  hormones is another one of those  massively complicated topics so let's  just leave it at that and if you want  more hormone related content let me know  in the comments below but speaking of a  massive topic reason number nine is that  you have a functional gi disorder so if  you've ruled out all of the above and  you're still experiencing bloating it  could be a sign that there may be a more  serious gastrointestinal disorder going  on some common digestive disorders that  can cause bloating include things like  irritable bowel syndrome ibs  inflammatory bowel disease ibd celiac  disease hypochloridia histamine  intolerance and pancreatic insufficiency  now i'm not going to get into the nitty  gritty on each of these but if you do  suspect there is a medical issue be  proactive and be pushy with your primary  health care provider to get the  appropriate tests run now moving on to  reason number 10 infection overgrowth or  dysbiosis now there are a number of  potential infections and overgrowths  that can potentially contribute to  digestive symptoms like bloating so  things like h pylori sibo c fo  c diff candida worms parasites or just  general dysbiosis in the gut the  diagnostic tools that we have for these  include things like breath tests like  you saw me do in my sibo series or gi  mapping or other stool samples that your  doctor can order from a lab in any case  do not follow some tick talkers protocol  and assume that you have like an  infection or an overgrowth without the  proper tests run because there are  pharmaceutical and herbal treatments for  these that are very specific to the  cause now reason number 11 is thyroid  dysfunction so the thyroid is so  important not only is it your metabolic  epicenter but it's also in charge of  communicating with every other system to  produce enough bile acid pancreatic acid  enzymes and to stimulate motility  you name it so folks with hypothyroidism  or hashimoto's often experience severe  digestive distress and bloating because  the thyroid receptors in the abdomen are  not getting enough thyroid hormone so  the gut isn't getting those digestive  signals as a result we see poor motility  which leads to constipation which means  the food has more time to ferment and  therefore a lot more gas and bloating  which also predisposes these folks to  other conditions like sibo and candida  in any case these symptoms usually  improve dramatically once we correct the  thyroid hormone reason number 12 trauma  to the brain gut axis now i've briefly  spoken about the brain gut axis before  but in short this is the bi-directional  communication between the central and  enteric nervous system that links  cognitive centers of the brain with  intestinal functioning it's a concept  behind the idea of having butterflies in  your stomach when you're nervous any  physical or emotional trauma that  damages this brain gut axis has the  power to cause bloating so this could be  actual physical trauma like a football  player's head injury or more  psychological trauma related to ptsd  depression or anxiety which is also  often related to low serotonin levels  now what about excess sodium and sugar  so we often use the term bloated to  describe a feeling when we eat like a  really salty meal or have a huge sugar  load but this puffy feeling  is more accurately described as water  retention in the case of salt high  sodium foods can cause our bodies to  retain excess water which can also  contribute to feeling puffy or in  colloquial terms bloated with  carbohydrates when consumed in excess  the energy that we don't immediately  need gets stored as glycogen along with  three grams of water for every gram of  carbohydrates stored so this explains  why people who go on really low carb  diets drop a ton of weight really  quickly it's a lot of water storage  weight from the glycogen depleting now  to close off i want to remind everyone  that this is not an exhaustive list of  causes and everyone's bloating  experience is going to be unique and  often multi-factorial but i do hope that  this gives you all a little bit of  insight into your own digestive patterns  and whether or not it's time to bring  your case to a skilled practitioner for  advice so on that note that is all that  i have for you guys today if you liked  it be sure to give it the thumbs up stay  tuned for part two in this bloating  episode don't forget to subscribe to  this channel and i will see you next  time on abby's kitchen  bye  [Music]
 

